From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:28:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Support 16K and 64K pages on arm64 build hosts

Soong links every musl host tool against libjemalloc5. With LG_PAGE 12
those tools abort at start on a 16K-page arm64 kernel (Apple silicon
Asahi) with "<jemalloc>: Unsupported system page size". Use 64K pages
for aarch64 hosts, which also works on 4K and 16K kernels.

Change-Id: I9290c287091c7b18155c242bcd31aa3f8db3782e
---
 include/jemalloc/internal/jemalloc_internal_defs_host.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/jemalloc/internal/jemalloc_internal_defs_host.h b/include/jemalloc/internal/jemalloc_internal_defs_host.h
index f4c973b..0cc5e80 100644
--- a/include/jemalloc/internal/jemalloc_internal_defs_host.h
+++ b/include/jemalloc/internal/jemalloc_internal_defs_host.h
@@ -199,7 +199,12 @@
 /* #undef LG_QUANTUM */
 
 /* One page is 2^LG_PAGE bytes. */
+#if defined(__aarch64__)
+/* arm64 kernels use 4K, 16K or 64K pages; jemalloc aborts on a larger one. */
+#define LG_PAGE 16
+#else
 #define LG_PAGE 12
+#endif
 
 /*
  * One huge page is 2^LG_HUGEPAGE bytes.  Note that this is defined even if the
